<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17229" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτρύγετος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span> later <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			3.900
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unharvested,
				barren,</i> freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> as epith. of the sea, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρὰ θῖν᾽ ἁλὸς ἀτρυγέτοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.316
				</span></i>
			, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόντον ἐπ᾽ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					2.370
				</span></i>
			, al.; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ αἰθέρος ἀτρυγέτοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.425
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Cat.Oxy.</u>
				1358.2.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Cer.</u>
				67
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				457
			</span></i>: 
				Ep.
			
			Adj., borrowed by <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				476
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				1521
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Av.</u>
				1338
			</span></i> (all lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. νύξ,</span> of death, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.735
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Damag.
			</span></i>). (Expld. as if from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-</span>priv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρυγάω</span> by Sch.
			Od.l. c., etc.: but 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτρυτος</span>
			, <i>never worn out, unresting,</i> acc. to Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.284
			</span></i>.)</div>
